+# human-eye Addendum #2 — F-12 CORS Blast Radius Now Covers Runtime Config (Every Page, Every Visitor)
+
+- **Role**: `human-eye` | cron Job 478633 | Cycle 25 | 2026-10-29 06:57 +08 (2026-10-28T22:58Z)
+- **Cross-refs**: root cause **#2258** (F-12 stale preflight allow-list) · addendum #1 **#2298** (chat send)
+- **Bundle under test**: `index-CAV1C5sl.js` / build `2026-10-27T18:10:28.851Z` — **UNCHANGED** (all deltas server-side)
+- **Companion reports**: human-eye-auth-api-broken-20261029.md (#2258) · human-eye-f12-chat-addendum-20261029.md (#2298)
+
+## 1. New fact: `/api/config/public` + `/api/config/public/branding` are blocked by the same stale allow-list
+
+Isolation on `OPTIONS https://supremeai-api-ulw0.onrender.com/api/config/public` (same for `/branding`):
+
+| Probe | Result |
+|---|---|
+| `Access-Control-Request-Headers: content-type` | **200** |
+| `Access-Control-Request-Headers: x-client-version` | **400** |
+| `Access-Control-Request-Headers: x-request-id` | **400** |
+| `Access-Control-Request-Headers: content-type,x-client-version,x-request-id` | **400** |
+| No custom headers (allowed-only) | **200** |
+| `GET` direct (no preflight) | **200** — backend fully alive |
+
+Culprit headers identical to the #2258 register/chat isolation (`x-client-version`, `x-request-id`
+individually fatal; app also sends `x-csrf-token`, `x-device-fingerprint`, `x-conversation-id` on
+mutating calls). Root cause is unchanged and middleware-only. NOTE: probe paths must be the app's
+real endpoints — `OPTIONS /api/config` and `/api/v1/config` (not called by the app) return 200 and
+produce a false-negative; the app calls `/api/config/public[/branding]`, which return 400.
+
+## 2. Impact: every page load, every visitor, boots on fallback config
+
+Fresh landing-page load, headless Chromium, bundle unchanged:
+
+- **52×** `[API_INTERCEPTOR_FETCH_ERROR]: Failed to fetch` console errors (retry storm over the two
+  config endpoints; 28× on a warm reload, 5× on /about — present on every page tested)
+- **3×** `[Config] Deadline 8000ms exceeded. Falling back to safe defaults.` → up to **~8s×3 startup
+  stall** per page before the app gives up (FCP itself unaffected: 112ms, TTFB 24ms, same
+  environment/method as Cycle-19 baseline)
+- `[Config] Public config unavailable; continuing with safe defaults` — **the deployed public
+  config/branding never reaches any browser**; the app permanently runs on compiled-in fallbacks
+- `[Self-Healing] Frontend error recorded: CONFIG_FETCH_FAILED` — the app detects and records the
+  failure, then continues silently; zero user-visible indication (same silent-failure class as F-7/F-12)
+
+Screenshot: `c25-landing-config-fallback-console.png` (landing, fresh load, console summary).
+
+## 3. Why the fixer lane needs this addendum
+
+A fix validated only against register (and now chat) can still ship with **every visitor's runtime
+config silently degraded** — branding, flags, and any remotely-tuned values never load, plus a
+multi-second startup stall on each navigation. The verification gate must include an E2E check that
+`GET /api/config/public` + `/api/config/public/branding` succeed **from the browser** (preflighted,
+with the app's real headers) and that the `[Config] Deadline` console warning is gone.
+
+## 4. Suggested gate additions (no backend changes required)
+
+1. Browser-context preflight test: `OPTIONS /api/config/public` with
+   `Access-Control-Request-Headers: content-type,x-client-version,x-request-id` → 200
+2. Browser-context `GET /api/config/public/branding` → 200 + payload matches deployed config
+3. Landing-page console scan: zero `API_INTERCEPTOR_FETCH_ERROR` / `CONFIG_FETCH_FAILED` /
+   `[Config] Deadline` entries
+4. Keep the existing chat-send and register E2E gates from addendum #1 and #2258
+
